  "result": "I added `median` to `src/core/median.ts` and committed it as `a1114b2`. `npm run fast` passed before the commit.\n\n- **Behavior:** it throws a `RangeError` on an empty list. It averages the middle pair for even-length lists and doesn't mutate its input.\n- **Tests:** `test/core/median.test.ts` covers odd length, even length, no mutation, and the empty-list rejection. I also added its weight to `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`.\n- **No helper reused:** the only existing median is a local closure in `src/outcome/ledger.ts` that handles nullable values. Core may only import from core, so I wrote `median` standalone.\n- **No task id:** the repo convention ends commit titles with the task id, but none was in my brief. The title is `Add a median helper to core that rejects an empty list`. Give me the id if you want me to amend it.",
